          %title Generic proofs
          %h1#generic_proofs Generic proofs
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#axioms_of_choice"} Axioms of choice
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong generic proof
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a map (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"}> morphism
            )
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Θ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta\colon \Theta\to\Lambda
            with all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
            such that, for every map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon Y\to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ν
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu\colon X\to \Lambda
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pulled back
            map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ν
                    %mo *
                  %mi θ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Θ
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Λ
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu^*\theta\;\colon\; \Theta \times_\Lambda X \to X
            each factor through each other, i.e. they are equivalent in the
            %span.newWikiWord
              preorder reflection
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/preorder+reflection"} ?
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Θ
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Λ
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi ν
                                %mo *
                              %mi θ
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mi ν
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Θ
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi θ
                        %mtd
                          %mi Λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array {
                  Y \\
                  \\uparrow \downarrow &amp; \searrow^f \\
                  \\Theta \times_\Lambda X &amp; \overset{\nu^*\theta}\longrightarrow &amp; X \\
                  \\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow\mathrlap{\nu} \\
                  \\Theta &amp; \overset{\theta}\longrightarrow &amp; \Lambda
                  }
          %p The main interest of generic proofs is in the following:
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ex%2Flex+completion"} ex/lex completion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi ex
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi lex
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has
              = succeed "s" do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  weak dependent product
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/weak+dependent+product"} ?
          %p
            In particular, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi ex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi lex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
            is a topos if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has a generic proof.
          %p
            A counterpart of generic proofs in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            is Russell’s
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                axiom of reducibility
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/axiom+of+reducibility"} ?
          %h2#axioms_of_choice Axioms of choice
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            satisfying the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
            is a generic proof, since any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon Y\to X
            factors through, and (assuming AC) is factored through by, its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi ex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi lex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
            is equivalent to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            The statement “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            has a generic proof,” or equivalently “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %mi ex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi lex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set_{ex/lex}
            is a topos,” is weaker than the full axiom of choice. Indeed,
            %a{:href => "#Menni2007"} Menni 2007
            shows that the exact completion of a Boolean Grothendieck topos with enough points is also a topos.
          %p
            An even weaker statement is “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %mi ex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi lex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set_{ex/lex}
            is
            = succeed ".\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-powered+category"} well-powered
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a set, then the subobject lattice of (the image of)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %mi ex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi lex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set_{ex/lex}
            is precisely the preorder reflection of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctors"} anafunctors
            between two small categories is essentially small.
          %p
            An instructive example is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi ex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi lex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Set^{\to}
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
            of
            = succeed "):" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            lacks a generic proof). It also shows, taking
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            to be the
            %span.newWikiWord
              coproduct completion
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/coproduct+completion"} ?
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+arrow"} walking arrow
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mi ex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_{ex}
            (which is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^\to
            here) a topos but
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mi ex
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (D_{ex})_{ex}
            not a topos. Details may be found in Menni’s
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Menni2"} 2003 paper
          %h2#references References
          %ul
